Bellows NEWS — History of user-visible changes.

Copyright (C) 2026 Kival
See the file COPYING for copying conditions.

Version 0.1.0 (2026-10-31)

  * Initial release of Bellows.
  * C++20 concept lattice (`tabular_source`, `estimator`,
    `supervised_fittable`, `unsupervised_fittable`, `predictor`,
    `belief_predictor`, `transformer`, `categorical_aware`,
    `missing_aware`, `tunable`, `serialisable`).
  * Unified `stagewise_booster` supporting exact and quantile-bin cuts,
    depth-synchronous, best-gain-frontier, and oblivious-symmetric tree
    growth, gradient-magnitude row filtering, ordered categorical
    statistics, and native missing-value routing.
  * Preprocessing transformers: `moment_normaliser`, `interval_rescaler`,
    `column_mender`, `indicator_expander`, `ordered_target_encoder`,
    `quantile_bucketer`, `dispersion_filter`, and `relevance_selector`.
  * Classical estimators: `penalised_linear_regressor`,
    `penalised_logistic_classifier`, `proximity_learner`,
    `gaussian_density_classifier`, `centroid_partitioner`, and
    `subspace_tree_ensemble`.
  * Composition and validation: `composite_chain` (`operator|`),
    `dynamic_chain`, `fold_splitter`, `stratified_splitter`,
    `cross_validate`, `parameter_sweep`, and composable evaluation
    metrics.
  * Versioned binary artefact serialisation and CLI tools (`bellows`,
    `bellows-train`, `bellows-infer`, `bellows-check`).
